# Gitignored files copied into every worktree Claude Code creates, for `--worktree`,
# for `EnterWorktree`, and for a subagent with `isolation: worktree`.
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout, so none of these are present in it, and each one
# fails in its own way, none of them naming the missing file:
#
#   pubspec_overrides.yaml   every sibling resolves from pub.dev instead, and the
#                            suite then certifies the PUBLISHED packages while you
#                            are editing the working trees. Nothing errors.
#   .env                     a bundled pubspec asset. flutter_dotenv defaults
#                            BROADCAST_CONNECTION to null on web and realtime never
#                            connects; `flutter analyze` reports it as
#                            asset_does_not_exist, which reads like a pubspec typo.
#   backend/.env             artisan aborts before it says why.
#   .artisan/plugins.json    every plugin command disappears from `./bin/fsa`.
#
# `.gitignore` syntax, and only files that match AND are gitignored are copied, so a
# tracked file can never be duplicated by this list.
#
# `bin/check` copies these plus `backend/public/build` and the worker's `.dev.vars`,
# because AGENTS.md offers `git worktree add` by hand as an equal path and that one
# reaches this file not at all. The overlap is deliberate.
#
# NOT processed when a WorktreeCreate hook replaces the default git logic; such a
# hook has to copy these itself. This project has no such hook, deliberately.
#
# One thing no file here can fix, because the rule lives in artisan:
# `sessionOwnershipError` treats a working directory INSIDE `projectRoot` as owning
# the session, and a worktree under `.claude/worktrees/` is inside the main
# checkout. So a `dusk:*` call from a worktree with no session of its own drives the
# app the MAIN checkout started, and reports success. Run `./bin/fsa start` in the
# worktree, or pass `--state=<path>`, before any dusk command there.

pubspec_overrides.yaml
.env
backend/.env
.artisan/plugins.json
